## Heading diagnostic

Heading is reported as a diagnostic because the current minimal-loss run sets the heading-loss weight to zero.

| Variant | HSR@15 | MHE (deg) |
|---|---:|---:|
| w/o GRU | 39.54% | 37.07 |
| w/o Kalman | 38.93% | 37.03 |
| w/o MeanShift | 38.46% | 38.22 |
| Full | 38.73% | 37.19 |

## Interpretation

- Full vs. w/o Kalman: MLE changes by +0.018 m, while jump rate changes from 0.746% to 0.543%.
- Three frames have the best MLE/P90 (3.952/7.052 m); the LSR@5 difference from one frame is not statistically resolved by the paired bootstrap.
- 6x6 is the balance point: only +0.029 m MLE behind 7x7, with 18.9% lower MeanShift latency.

## Integrity audit

`STRICT_ALL_METRICS_FULL_BEST=FAIL`

Do not claim that Full wins every metric. The measured result supports GRU and MeanShift for localization, three frames for MLE/P90, and Kalman for lower jump rate; the no-Kalman MLE advantage is 0.018 m.

